# DualMind Arena — AI Agent Rules

## What this repo is

DualMind Arena is a **vanilla-JS AI model battle arena**. Users compare two LLM responses side-by-side, vote, and build a leaderboard. Static HTML/CSS/JS is served by Cloudflare Workers; an Azure backend handles `/api/*`; Supabase handles client-side auth.

## Golden rules

1. **Read `AGENTS.md` before any major change.** It contains the canonical file map, event bus, globals, and design-token rules.
2. **Do not import deprecated shims.** Use `js/apiInstance.js` for API calls; use `js/auth/supabase-auth.js` for auth; the app orchestrator is `js/ui/app.js`.
3. **Keep `window` globals minimal.** If a new global is unavoidable, add it to the AGENTS.md Window Globals table.
4. **Sanitize HTML that touches user or AI content.** Use `DOMPurify` (already loaded) or React/Vue-safe rendering.
5. **Stick to the design tokens.** `#4AABC2` and layout offsets must come from `css/tokens.css` variables.
6. **No `console.log` in production paths.** Use `console.warn`/`console.error` only for real errors.
7. **Run the tooling after changes.** Fix the lint glob first (`package.json` line 9 needs quotes around `--ignore-pattern "admin-email-system/**"`).

## Quick commands

```bash
npm install          # dependencies
npm run dev          # http://localhost:8000
npm run lint         # broken out-of-box; fix glob quoting first
npm run test         # broken; playwright is not installed
npm run build        # build.js -> ./dist
npm run deploy       # build + wrangler deploy
```

## Architecture at a glance

```
Browser
  ├─ config.js              → window.DUALMIND_CONFIG
  ├─ js/auth/supabase-init.js  → window.DualMindAuth / window.DualMindAuthReady
  ├─ js/ui/app.js           → main App class (window._APP)
  │    ├─ components/Header.js
  │    ├─ components/Sidebar.js
  │    ├─ components/ChatInput.js
  │    └─ components/chat/ChatView.js
  └─ js/apiInstance.js      → api singleton (window._DUALMIND_API)

Cloudflare Worker (worker.js)
  ├─ /api/*   → Azure backend
  ├─ /share/* → share/index.html
  └─ /*       → ASSETS binding (dist/)
```

## What NOT to do

- Do not touch prototypes: `App.jsx`, `next-dualmind/`, `old-html-backup/`, `arena-core.js`.
- Do not import `js/api-client.js`, `js/auth.js`, or `js/auth/api-service.js` in new code.
- Do not add inline `<style>` or hardcoded hex colors in JS templates.
- Do not put real secrets in `config.js`.

## Known traps

- `login/auth-complete.js` is currently broken (undefined `emailInput`, `setLoading`, `supabaseClient`, `SITE_URL`). Any auth change here must fix those references first.
- `process.env` in `config.js` does **not** work in the browser; config must come from build-time replacement or env injection.
- The worker sets `Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *`; restrict it to real origins before production.
